  "reviews": {
    "observed": "Live selected-bank mutation has a final callback or a completed compound scope. Generic affects, wards, refresh, expiry, cures, binding, wake, damage release, conversion and staff edits are observed without accepted-application or caster credit.",
    "construction": "Fresh/unpublished character or NPC lifetime before admission. Temporary account/deletion/display loads cannot pass the live runtime identity guard. Constructor banks establish the first admitted baseline; they are not gameplay changes to an earlier lifetime.",
    "admission": "enter_game restores/rebuilds a new admitted lifetime before game_enter/session observation; reconnect uses the existing connection-transition path. Initial bank clearing in init_char precedes placement. Baseline is taken after entry. Copyover closes the old producer and establishes a fresh target baseline.",
    "aggregate": "apply_affs is called only by all_affects. FALSE is a temporary removal phase; all maintained live remove/reapply callers have an outer scope. TRUE/all affect insertion/removal publishes the completed bank state. Object and effect bitvectors are inputs to these boundaries, not independent live banks.",
    "offset": "Staff offset tables reach the actual character-bank copy/parser boundary. sa_intCopy observes the affected offset; setbit_parseTable observes only character aff/aff2 rows after the copy, excluding object/effect/room tables.",
    "unchanged": "Only non-selected hide/invisible/concealment bits change. Faerie fog saves and restores the same selected bits; actual effect removal delegates to the generic observed removal path."
  },
